 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation: Elvira's \"Chi è\" is sung in the last bar of the Trio before (Ah! chi mi dice mai) and is not in this score, so her first phrase is \"là?\"; \"sei qui?\", \"azion si nera\", \"calmate questa collera\" (libretto quella), \"del ciel\", \"e lasci in preda\" (libretto e mi lasci), \"per pena\", \"sono\", \"volle\", \"fa presto\", Leporello's \"conciossiacosa quando fosse che Il quadro\" as printed (four words, capital Il), \"fuggi!\" and \"m'inganno,\" without the accents of fuggì and ingannò (IPA as sung: fudˈdʒi, miŋ.ganˈnɔ). The asides keep the print's brackets. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S07) and the IPA was checked against Castel. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
